{{also|ki'u}}
==Esperanto==

===Etymology===
{{m|eo|ki-||interrogative and relative [[:Category:Esperanto correlatives|correlative]] prefix}} + {{m|eo|-u||correlative suffix of individuals}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Eo-kiu.ogg|Audio|lang=eo}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|eo|pronoun|cat2=correlatives|plural|kiuj|accusative singular|kiun|accusative plural|kiujn}}

# [[who]] (the interrogative and relative correlative of individuals)
#: ''Mi jam diris, ke mia frato, '''kiu''' estis iomete pli aĝa ol mi, mortis.''
#:: I already said, that my brother, '''who''' was a little bit older than me, died.
# {{lb|eo|relative}} [[which]]
#: ''La vivo moviĝas laŭ bova rapideco sur la sunaj, ĉielgloraj deklivoj, '''kiuj''' falas de la piramidaj pintoj al la bordoj de la bluega oceano.''
#:: Life moves ploddingly on the sunny, heavenly-glorious slopes, '''which''' fall from the piramidal peaks to the borders of the big blue ocean.
#: ''Karlo restas fama pro la influo-batalo, kiun li entreprenis kontraŭ la Parlamento de Anglio.''<sup>[http://eo.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karlo_la_1-a_(Anglio)]</sup>
#:: Charles remains famous for the influence battle, '''which''' he undertook against the English Parliament.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|eo|kiu ajn|gloss=[[whoever]]}}

===Determiner===
{{eo-det}}

# [[which]], [[what]]

===Usage notes===
Like other interrogative and relative correlatives, '''kiu''' can be combined with {{m|eo|ajn}}, the adverbial particle of generality. '''Kiu ajn''' thus means ''[[whoever]]''.

